<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson chartering planes to Philippines.</title>
<headline>Ericsson chartering planes to Philippines.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecoms firm LM Ericsson AB has chartered three Antonov-124 cargo planes to cope with freight shipments from Sweden to the Philippines, a market source said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;It has happened three times since October 27. I think it was sea cargo which was sent by air because of a delay,&quot; the source told Reuters.</p>
<p>The source did not specify where Ericsson was chartering the planes, which have a cargo capacity of between 110 and 120 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
